

/*!
   \page lua-wrapper-api.html overview

	\title Lua Wrapper API

	\indexpage Lua Wrapper API
	\startpage Lua Wrapper API
	\ingroup lua

	The Elysian Shadows engine contains an embedded Lua interpreter, allowing the engine to be extended through the use of Lua scripting. The engine is currently using version 5.2 of the Lua interpreter as the scripting core, OOLua to create bindings between C++ and Lua, and a custom DSL by Falco for creating a full property system to expose native C++ objects as standard Lua tables.

	\section1 Design Philosophy

	\section1 Extending the Engine
	Lua code can be loaded and executed through several different mechanisms, depending on the script's requirements.
	\list
	\li \b {global_init.lua} - script that gets executed when the engine loads
	\li \b {level_init.lua} - script that gets executed when a level is loaded
	\li \b {area_init.lua} - script that gets executed when an area is loaded
	\li \b {Lua Behaviors} - script that gets attached to an entity has a Behavior component
	\li \b {Lua Debug Console} - dynamically executes code for debugging and testing purposes
	\endlist

	\section1 Logging and Error Handling

	\section1 Debugging Scripts

	\section1 Toolkit-Specific Features and Utilities

	\section1 Example Lua Scripts
	Several Demo areas have been bundled within ESTk to provide examples of how to interact with the various Engine
	features and functionality via the Lua API. For the full list of these levels, please visit the 
	\l {Example Areas} page of the ESToolkit Documentation.



	\section1 External Lua Documentation
	\list
	\li Official Lua Docs
	\li OOLua Documentation
	\endlist


